# Per-stack config (Pulumi.<stack>.yaml) holds environment-specific settings and
# encrypted secrets; the Pulumi Cloud backend is the source of truth. Only the
# project file (Pulumi.yaml) is committed.
Pulumi.*.yaml
!Pulumi.yaml
# vitruvian-tabs's stack configs are deliberately committed (config-as-code, like
# repo_config's Pulumi.dev.yaml): they hold only non-secret identifiers
# (project id, region, deployer SA email, adoption flags). Runtime secrets
# stay in GCP Secret Manager.
!apps/vitruvian-tabs/Pulumi.*.yaml
# oauth-user-inspector's PER-APP stacks (app + deploy identity) live co-located
# under oauth-user-inspector/infra/ (repo-wide convention: <app>/infra/ holds
# per-app deployment infra); their stack-config policy is replicated by
# oauth-user-inspector/infra/.gitignore — which now also covers the shared
# -build stack, relocated there so all three of the app's stacks sit together.
# zitadel-apps commits its dev stack config (non-secret Zitadel org/project/app
# identifiers + redirect URIs) so the deploy workflow resolves them on a clean
# checkout. The Zitadel machine-user credential is injected from a pipeline
# secret at apply time, never committed.
!platform/zitadel-apps/Pulumi.*.yaml
# zitadel-apps-mcp-slack commits its stack config for the same reason: non-secret
# Zitadel identifiers (project/app/role names, the role-check flag). The client id
# and secret it mints are stack OUTPUTS held in Pulumi Cloud state, not config, so
# nothing sensitive is committed here either.
!platform/zitadel-apps-mcp-slack/Pulumi.*.yaml
# zitadel-apps-relay: same — non-secret Zitadel identifiers only.
!platform/zitadel-apps-relay/Pulumi.*.yaml
# zitadel-mcp-viewer: same — org id and PAT expiry date only. The PAT itself is a
# secret stack output in Pulumi Cloud state.
!platform/zitadel-mcp-viewer/Pulumi.*.yaml
# platform/stripe commits its stack config: non-secret Stripe settings (mode,
# currency, donation amounts, app list). The Stripe key is STRIPE_API_KEY in CI
# or Pulumi ciphertext locally; a test rejects a plaintext key in the file.
!platform/stripe/Pulumi.*.yaml
# platform/pagerduty commits its stack config: non-secret PagerDuty settings
# (responder email, escalation policy, service list). The PagerDuty token is
# PAGERDUTY_TOKEN in CI or Pulumi ciphertext locally; a test rejects a
# plaintext token in the file.
!platform/pagerduty/Pulumi.production.yaml
# platform/sentry commits its stack config: non-secret Sentry settings
# (base URL, organization, team, project list). The Sentry token is
# SENTRY_TOKEN in CI or Bitwarden locally; a test rejects a plaintext token,
# non-allowlisted `secure:` value, or unknown config key in the file.
!platform/sentry/Pulumi.production.yaml
# platform/sentry-pagerduty commits its stack config: non-secret Sentry and
# PagerDuty wiring settings. The Sentry token is SENTRY_TOKEN or Pulumi
# ciphertext locally, and the PagerDuty routing key is read via StackReference;
# a test rejects a plaintext token in the file.
!platform/sentry-pagerduty/Pulumi.production.yaml
# foundation/gcp-bootstrap commits its production stack config: only non-secret
# identifiers (org id, billing account id, group emails, parent folder id,
# github owner, the co-tenancy gate flag). It has no secret config keys (the
# monorepo WIF adaptation removed the github token path), so nothing sensitive
# is committed. Backend is Pulumi Cloud.
!foundation/gcp-bootstrap/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/org-folders commits its stack config: only the org id (non-secret).
!foundation/org-folders/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-org commits its production stack config: org id, billing
# account, bootstrap stack ref, governance groups, domains — all non-secret.
# The Pulumi project root lives at envs/shared (upstream 1-org/envs/shared layout).
!foundation/gcp-org/envs/shared/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-environments commits per-environment stack configs: org id,
# billing account, org stack ref, parent folder — all non-secret. Each
# environment is its own leaf Pulumi project under envs/ (upstream
# 2-environments/envs/<env> layout) with a single `production` stack; the env
# identity is pinned in each leaf's main.go.
!foundation/gcp-environments/envs/*/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-networks commits per-leaf stack configs: org id, regions,
# org stack ref, network config, firewall rules — all non-secret. Each leaf
# (shared hub + the development/nonproduction/production spokes) is its own
# leaf Pulumi project under envs/ (upstream 3-networks-hub-and-spoke/envs/<env>
# layout) with a single `production` stack; the env identity and spoke CIDR
# plan are pinned in each leaf's main.go.
!foundation/gcp-networks/envs/*/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-projects commits per-leaf stack configs:
# business code, billing account, env stack ref, project-type toggles — all
# non-secret. Each business-unit leaf (shared + development/nonproduction/
# production) is its own leaf Pulumi project under business_unit_1/ (upstream
# 4-projects/business_unit_1/<leaf> layout) with a single `production` stack;
# the env identity is pinned in each leaf's main.go. These MUST be committed
# (not gitignored) so required config resolves on a clean checkout.
!foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_1/*/Pulumi.*.yaml
!foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_2/*/Pulumi.*.yaml
# foundation/gcp-app-infra commits per-leaf stack configs: the cross-stage stack
# names, business code, region, and the app list. No secrets — the deploy
# identity's grants are code, and image digests are per-invocation inputs.
!foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_1/*/Pulumi.*.yaml
!foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_2/*/Pulumi.*.yaml

# Compiled Pulumi program binary left behind by `go build .` (the binary is
# named after the module's last path element, i.e. "pulumi").
/pulumi
# Per-project program binary left behind by a stray `go build .` in the project
# dir (named after that module's last path element). (The old /zitadel-apps/
# path predates the platform/ move and matched nothing — which is how the
# binary got committed.)
platform/zitadel-apps/zitadel-apps
platform/zitadel-apps-mcp-slack/zitadel-apps-mcp-slack
platform/zitadel-apps-relay/zitadel-apps-relay
platform/zitadel-mcp-viewer/zitadel-mcp-viewer
platform/pagerduty/pagerduty
platform/sentry/sentry
platform/sentry-pagerduty/sentry-pagerduty
/foundation/gcp-bootstrap/foundation-0-bootstrap
/foundation/org-folders/foundation-org-folders
/foundation/gcp-org/envs/shared/foundation-org-shared
/foundation/gcp-org/envs/shared/foundation-org
/foundation/gcp-environments/envs/development/foundation-environments-development
/foundation/gcp-environments/envs/nonproduction/foundation-environments-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-environments/envs/production/foundation-environments-production
/foundation/gcp-networks/envs/shared/foundation-networks-shared
/foundation/gcp-networks/envs/development/foundation-networks-development
/foundation/gcp-networks/envs/nonproduction/foundation-networks-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-networks/envs/production/foundation-networks-production
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_1/shared/foundation-projects-bu1-shared
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_1/development/foundation-projects-bu1-development
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_1/nonproduction/foundation-projects-bu1-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_1/production/foundation-projects-bu1-production
/foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_1/development/foundation-app-infra-bu1-development
/foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_2/development/foundation-app-infra-bu2-development
/foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_2/nonproduction/foundation-app-infra-bu2-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_2/production/foundation-app-infra-bu2-production
/foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_1/nonproduction/foundation-app-infra-bu1-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-app-infra/business_unit_1/production/foundation-app-infra-bu1-production
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_2/shared/foundation-projects-bu2-shared
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_2/development/foundation-projects-bu2-development
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_2/nonproduction/foundation-projects-bu2-nonproduction
/foundation/gcp-projects/business_unit_2/production/foundation-projects-bu2-production


# Compiled Go pulumi-program binary (bazel/go build output) — never track.
